**Notes on things I did not fully implement / simplified:**

- **Score-table rows on the title screen** show a single "X / Y" value per enemy type rather than four separate columns (formation / diving / escort bonuses) — space is tight at 224 px.
- The **captured fighter's firing while its boss dives** uses a low random rate rather than precise arcade cadence, and freed-dock timing is approximate.
- **Escort geometry during tractor beams** is simplified (escorts hover beside the beam base); they are not rendered as a full formation cluster.
- Boss "recolor after first hit" is shown with a translucent blue tint overlay instead of swapping to a fully re-authored purple sprite sheet.
- The ram-collision half-selection when only one dual-fighter half exists can occasionally mark the wrong half; functionally the player still loses exactly one ship.

Everything else in the spec — fixed-timestep loop, 2-shot limit, curved entry paths with per-group waves, breathing/swaying formation, diving escorts, tractor beam + capture + dual fighter (with the "shoot-in-formation kills the captive" rule), challenging stages at 3/7/11… with wave bonuses and PERFECT!, arcade stage badges, hit-results screen, extra ships at 20k then every 70k, synthesized SFX with M-mute, localStorage high score, READY respawn gating dives, and crisp pixel scaling — is implemented.
